    ],
    "notes": "non-canonical or out-of-range muxed account ids (uint64, 0 to 2^64-1). accepted cases carry the M address and MuxedAccount XDR for key 0x3a..3a with that id. text is accepted only as the exact decimal rendering of an in-range value (ASCII digits, no sign, whitespace, leading zero, radix prefix, fraction or exponent); a JSON number is accepted as an integer in range with |n| <= 2^53-1, and refused when negative, fractional or out of range. in-range JSON numbers above 2^53-1 are in a separate implementation-defined entry. negative offer ids are refused because core answers MANAGE_SELL_OFFER_MALFORMED / MANAGE_BUY_OFFER_MALFORMED for offerID < 0 from protocol 15 (stellar-core v30.0.0 src/transactions/ManageOfferOpFrameBase.cpp, ManageOfferOpFrameBase::doCheckValid). the reject reason is informational; a testee passes by refusing.",
